<title>USA: Georgia Power sees nuke back later Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Georgia Power sees nuke back later Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Georgia Power Co's 1,162 megawatt (MW) Vogtle 2 nuclear unit, which was manually shut late Monday, is expected to restart later today, the company said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's pretty minor. They think it will be back on-line later today,&quot; said company spokeswoman Loretto Stevens.</p>
<p>The unit, located in Waynesboro, Ga., was shut due to a &quot;malfunctioning feedwater regulator valve,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>Georgia Power's other Vogtle unit, with an identical generating capacity, is operating at full power.</p>
<p>Georgia Power is a unit of Southern Co.</p>
<p>--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
